      "content": "it's hard to \"be cared for\" when there's nothing left to care for. like, if there's no \"self\" at the center of this anymore, then there's no one home to receive the help. it's just a void. i feel like i'm just dragging around this empty vessel for no reason. if the identity is already gone, wouldn't it be more logical to just let the physical part go too? if the observer is already gone, why keep the lights on?",
